*Critical Climate Change Adaptation example:*

*Ecosystem Zone Marina Alta*
*Focus on Cherries (failure in non-irrigated farms), also review olive oil
(production down), almonds (also a climate change pest failure).
Suggestions for crop changes pistachios, *


Olive, almond, and cherry trees in the Alicante Mountains form a highly
interdependent, terraced dry-stone ecosystem adapted to rocky soils and
variable Mediterranean microclimates. These centuries-old agricultural
systems balance biodiversity with extreme vulnerability to climate shifts
and disease.

Increased biodiversity will increase ecosystem service scores such as water
soil retention, stability, nutrients, reduced evaporation, pollination,
ecotourism (trekking) etc. see Danube.
There is an aquifer which runs underground in the region
Drip irrigation is likely to be a key solution to tree crop production, but
not so easy to administer in mountain terraces and has consequences for
disposable fresh water volume, is there publically available data to
evaluate this?
For the Cherry trees pollinating trees are flowering at different time to
those trees needed pollination.

Key Ecosystem Zones & Elevations

   - *Upper Mountain Valleys (500m - 900m altitude):*
      - *Core Crop:* Cherries (*Cerezas de la Monta=C3=B1a de Alicante*,
      protected under a Protected Geographical Indication).
      - *Locations:* Grown extensively in northern inland municipalities
      like *Vall de Gallinera*, *Vall d'Alcal=C3=A0*, *Beniarr=C3=A9s*, *Al=
fafara*,
      and *Pen=C3=A1guila*.
      - *Conditions:* Requires 13=C2=B0C to 15.5=C2=B0C average annual temp=
eratures.
      These microclimates feature higher rainfall than the coast, but
the terrain
      is rugged with high calcium carbonate soil and little organic matter.
      - *Ecosystem Links:* Hand-harvested via artisanal methods. The
      orchards rely on spontaneous native flora along dry-stone terraces to
      maintain soil moisture and prevent erosion. [1
      <https://www.freshplaza.com/europe/article/9842436/spain-allocates-us=
-1-66-million-in-climate-aid-for-cherry-growers/>,
      2 <https://565msnm.com/en/pages/la-finca>, 3
      <https://www.montiboli.com/en/blog/cherries-in-alicante/>, 4
      <https://foodandtravel.com/travel/news/paradise-valley-vall-de-la-gal=
linera>,
      5
      <https://www.spain-holiday.com/Pego/articles/explore-cherry-orchards-=
and-prehistoric-cave-paintings-in-alicante>
      ]
   - *Mid-Altitude Terraces (100m - 500m altitude):*
      - *Core Crops:* Almonds (*Almendros*) and Mountain Olives (*Olivos de
      Monta=C3=B1a*).
      - *Locations:* Valleys such as *Vall de Gallinera*, *Vall de
      Jal=C3=B3n/Xal=C3=B3*, *Guadalest*, and *Relleu*.
      - *Conditions:* Soil is structured via irregular, winding, dry-stone
      retaining walls. Olive varieties indigenous to the area, such as
      *Alfafarenca* and *Blanqueta*, dominate.
      - *Ecosystem Links:* Olives are sturdy, requiring minimal
      intervention and thriving in dry conditions, whereas almonds have
      traditionally been a rainfed crop requiring winter chilling to bloom
      between January and March. [1
      <https://www.montiboli.com/en/blog/routes-almonds-in-bloom-alicante/>=
,
      2 <https://connectingvalencia.com/marina-alta/la-vall-de-gallinera/>,
      3
      <https://www.wiberrentacar.com/blog/en/alicante-bloom-visiting-almond=
-trees/>,
      4
      <https://ithacabound.com/30000-olive-trees-a-visit-to-almazara-la-alq=
ueria/>,
      5
      <https://food.soledadpenades.com/2021/10/10/our-visit-to-almazara-la-=
alqueria-an-olive-oil-mill-in-alicante/>,
      6
      <https://www.abahanavillas.com/en/leisure-costa-blanca/sports-and-adv=
entures-costa-blanca/almond-and-cherry-blossoms-on-the-costa-blanca>,
      7 <https://565msnm.com/en/pages/la-finca>]

Current Environmental Pressures & Ecological Crises

   - *Xylella fastidiosa Bacteria:* Almond ecosystems have been severely
   impacted by the aggressive Xylella fastidiosa outbreak, leading to the
   felling and clearing of hundreds of thousands of infected trees across
   places like *T=C3=A0rbena* and *Alcalal=C3=AD*. Because there is no cure=
, farmers
   are shifting away from almonds to avoid total collapse, sometimes
   diversifying into hardier carob production. [1
   <https://viewfromlavila.com/almond-blossom-time-on-the-costa-blanca/>, 2
   <https://biovexo.eu/biovexo-going-alicante/>]
   - *Climate Change & Pests:*
      - Extended droughts and altered winter chilling hours have severely
      impacted both almonds and cherries.
      - Cherry yields have suffered drops of up to 70% in non-irrigated
      zones due to heat stress and the *Drosophila suzukii* pest.
      - To combat climate and water availability issues, farms at lower
      altitudes have shifted away from traditional tree crops, with
some regions
      replacing olive trees with more profitable, drought-resistant
alternatives
      like pistachios. [1
      <https://cherrytimes.it/en/news/Bad-season-for-the-Alicante-mountain-=
cherry-more-than-70-percent-of-the-harvest-lost>,
      2 <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DiOWqSyQTiwk&t=3D1>, 3
      <https://bexylproject.org/updates/spanish-press-xf-and-drought-put-al=
icante-almond-at-risk-of-extinction/>
      ]

Agro-Tourism and Generational Renewal

   - *Agro-Ecotourism:* The flowering seasons are massive economic drivers.
   Almond blossom walks in *Valle de Jal=C3=B3n* and cherry blossoms in *Va=
ll de
   Gallinera* draw thousands of eco-tourists. Events like *Feslal=C3=AD* in
   *Alcalal=C3=AD* celebrate local almond gastronomy. [1
   <https://www.montiboli.com/en/blog/routes-almonds-in-bloom-alicante/>, 2
   <https://www.abahanavillas.com/en/leisure-costa-blanca/sports-and-advent=
ures-costa-blanca/almond-and-cherry-blossoms-on-the-costa-blanca>,
   4
   <https://foodandtravel.com/travel/news/paradise-valley-vall-de-la-gallin=
era>
   ]
   - *Regenerative Initiatives:* Local producers and young farmers are
   attempting to recover neglected plots using regenerative agriculture=E2=
=80=94using
   handheld branch shakers and spontaneous ground cover to preserve natural
   balance. The regional government (*Generalitat*) is subsidizing land
   recovery (=E2=82=AC230,000 recently injected into areas like l'Alcoi=C3=
=A0) to save the
   iconic mountain cherry industry. [1
   <https://565msnm.com/en/pages/la-finca>, 2
   <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3D5d6HyNS_VyA>, 3
   <https://www.democrata.es/en/agriculture-food/agriculture-reinforces-its=
