&surface=3D%7Bsurface%7D&funnel=3D%7Bfunnel%7D&google_ads_click_source=3D%7=
BGOOGLE-ADS-CLICK-SOURCE%7D&product_id=3D%7Bproduct_id%7D&option_id=3D%7Bop=
tion_id%7D&partner_id=3DCD951>
   ]


Alicante's mountain cherry sector is facing a severe crisis marked by
consecutive poor harvests driven by prolonged drought, unusual cold cycles,
and pests. The Young Farmers' Agricultural Association of Alicante (*Asaja
Alicante*) and local authorities are currently deploying emergency aid and
generational renewal packages to rescue the Protected Geographical
Indication (PGI) crop. [1
<https://cherrytimes.it/en/news/Bad-season-for-the-Alicante-mountain-cherry=
-more-than-70-percent-of-the-harvest-lost>,
2
<https://cherrytimes.it/en/news/PGI-Alicante-cherries-in-trouble-with-a-sea=
son-expecting-half-the-harvest-quantities>,
3
<https://smartcherry.world/countries/spain/bad-season-for-the-alicante-moun=
tain-cherry-more-than-70-of-the-harvest-lost/>,
4
<https://www.todoalicante.es/english/alicante-cherry-industry-seeks-2026053=
0100523-nt.html>,
5
<https://www.freshplaza.com/europe/article/9842436/spain-allocates-us-1-66-=
million-in-climate-aid-for-cherry-growers/>,
6
<https://diarivalencia.cat/en/l-alacanti/general/generalitat-boosts-alicant=
e-mountain-cherries-with-aid>
]
=F0=9F=93=89 Key Challenges & Production Impact

   - *Harvest Decline:* Production has plummeted well below historical
   averages. Output has suffered heavily, failing to reach normal threshold=
s
   due to erratic weather patterns and the *Drosophila suzukii* pest. [1
   <https://cherrytimes.it/en/news/castellon-cherries-rebound-production-15=
00-tonnes>,
   2
   <https://cherrytimes.it/en/news/Bad-season-for-the-Alicante-mountain-che=
rry-more-than-70-percent-of-the-harvest-lost>,
   3
   <https://cherrytimes.it/en/news/PGI-Alicante-cherries-in-trouble-with-a-=
season-expecting-half-the-harvest-quantities>,
   4
   <https://smartcherry.world/countries/spain/bad-season-for-the-alicante-m=
ountain-cherry-more-than-70-of-the-harvest-lost/>
   ]
   - *Structural Strain:* The combination of low yields, high operational
   costs (diesel, self-employment fees), and climate unpredictability has l=
ed
   to the progressive abandonment of traditional orchards in inland mountai=
n
   regions like *l'Alcoi=C3=A0* and *Marina Alta*. [1
   <https://www.foodswinesfromspain.com/en/food/products/fruits---vegetable=
s/cerezas-de-la-montana-de-alicante-pgi>,
   2
   <https://cherrytimes.it/en/news/Bad-season-for-the-Alicante-mountain-che=
rry-more-than-70-percent-of-the-harvest-lost>,
   3
   <https://smartcherry.world/countries/spain/bad-season-for-the-alicante-m=
ountain-cherry-more-than-70-of-the-harvest-lost/>,
   4
   <https://www.freshplaza.com/europe/article/9842436/spain-allocates-us-1-=
66-million-in-climate-aid-for-cherry-growers/>
   ]

=F0=9F=92=B6 Generational Renewal & Subsidies
To counteract the decline and attract young growers to the *Cerezas de la
Monta=C3=B1a de Alicante PGI*, local governments have rolled out significan=
t
financial relief: [1
<https://www.freshplaza.com/europe/article/9842436/spain-allocates-us-1-66-=
million-in-climate-aid-for-cherry-growers/>,
2
<https://www.foodswinesfromspain.com/en/food/products/fruits---vegetables/c=
erezas-de-la-montana-de-alicante-pgi>,
3
<https://diarivalencia.cat/en/l-alacanti/general/generalitat-boosts-alicant=
e-mountain-cherries-with-aid>
]

   - The Valencian Community has approved hundreds of aid packages totaling
   tens of millions of euros.
   - Within Alicante province, dozens of grants have been specifically
   dedicated to young farmers and new entrants to prevent the loss of
   agricultural heritage. [1
   <https://www.freshplaza.com/europe/article/9842436/spain-allocates-us-1-=
66-million-in-climate-aid-for-cherry-growers/>,
   2
   <https://diarivalencia.cat/en/l-alacanti/general/generalitat-boosts-alic=
ante-mountain-cherries-with-aid>
   ]

=F0=9F=8D=92 Industry Response & Fairs
