For Bro. It's confusing but note that e.g. for the purpose of funding,
Climate Change Adaptation (in a sense creating resilience to climate change
in natural and human systems) is different to Climate Change Mitigation
(reduction in carbon emissions). So carbon credits do not directly support
climate change adaptation objectives, they are specifically tied to
reduction in carbon emissions which has very specific accounting e.g.
number and growth rate of additional trees planted after a 1990 baseline,
mechanical Direct Air Capture of carbon dioxide.
