ALGARROBO

Yes, carob (*algarrobo*) is a classic, deeply traditional tree crop for the
Alicante mountain regions. Thriving in the rocky, calcareous, and arid
terrain characteristic of the Valencian Community, carob trees are highly
resilient, drought-tolerant, and perfectly adapted to the shifting
Mediterranean climate. [1
<https://www.facebook.com/groups/uniquetrees/posts/1857154734922189/>, 2
<https://wildsideholidays.co.uk/carob-tree-ceratonia-siliqua-algarrobo/>, 3
<https://residenciaestates.com/carob-tree-unsung-hero/>, 4
<https://www.hernandorena.com/en/carob-tree-proyect/>, 5
<https://terrasafe.eu/2026/01/30/carob-a-future-food-that-can-grow-in-dryla=
nd-areas/>
]
Why Carobs Fit the Alicante Mountains

   - *Climate Resilience:* Requiring as little as 350 mm of rainfall
   annually, carobs easily withstand hot, baking Costa Blanca summers and
   rocky mountain slopes. [1
   <https://cyclingcountry.com/travel/mediterranean-carob-tree-mallorcas-us=
eful-plant/>,
   2
   <https://scalar.usc.edu/works/plants-and-people/carob-from-pod-to-pantry=
>,
   3 <https://mtb-touren-costablanca.regiondo.de/e-mtb-camp-244621>, 4
   <https://terrasafe.eu/2026/01/30/carob-a-future-food-that-can-grow-in-dr=
yland-areas/>
   ]
   - *Soil Adaptation:* They flourish on marginal, shallow, and degraded
   limestone soils where other crops like citrus or stone fruits struggle. =
[
   1
   <https://terrasafe.eu/2026/01/30/carob-a-future-food-that-can-grow-in-dr=
yland-areas/>,
   2 <https://www.hernandorena.com/en/carob-tree-proyect/>]
   - *Ecological Value:* Mature deep-root systems help prevent severe soil
   erosion on steep hillsides, also serving as natural firebreaks in mounta=
in
   forests. [1 <https://puebloman.com/2014/07/08/carob/>, 2
   <https://www.malaga.es/en/laprovincia/naturaleza/lis_cd-13057/carob-tree=
-ceratonia-siliqua>,
   3
   <https://cyclingcountry.com/travel/mediterranean-carob-tree-mallorcas-us=
eful-plant/>
   ]

